    L1(abs_all(xs), y) = 12   L1(running_max(xs), y) = 8   (review: 12 and 8 on its one row)
    DL(y | abs_all(xs)) = 27 bits   DL(y | running_max(xs)) = 26 bits
    size-2 list classes: 27, L1 defined for 14
      abs_all(xs)  [on the path]     L1 rank  3 of 14   DL rank  8 of 27   label bound h = 1  -> KEPT by labels at n* = 4
      running_max(xs) [off the path] L1 rank  2 of 14   DL rank  4 of 27   label bound h = 1  -> KEPT by labels at n* = 4
      labels rule out 0 of the 27 size-2 list classes at n* = 4
      five closest by L1: running_sum(xs) (3), running_max(xs) (8), inc_all(xs) (12), abs_all(xs) (12), sort(xs) (12)
      unary chains g(f(running_max(xs))) that equal y: 0  (so the labels keep a class that cannot be completed)

